      "In an era of rapid social change, a sense of social responsibility has become indispensable rather than optional. It refers to the awareness that our choices affect others and the willingness to act for the common good. Far from being an empty moral slogan, it is the very foundation on which individuals grow and communities thrive.",
      "First and foremost, social responsibility drives personal growth. When students volunteer in nursing homes or join campus clean-up campaigns, they cultivate empathy, discipline and leadership that no textbook can teach. What is more, it holds society together. During the pandemic, countless ordinary people delivered supplies and staffed testing sites, and it was precisely this collective sense of duty that kept cities running. Without such commitment, public trust would collapse and every individual would eventually pay the price.",
      "In conclusion, a sense of social responsibility matters because it shapes better citizens and a more harmonious society. We should therefore start with small deeds—recycling, helping a neighbor, or speaking up for the vulnerable—and let responsibility become a habit rather than a duty."
